<title>FRANCE: French truckers protest working conditions.</title>
<headline>French truckers protest working conditions.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Truckers snarled traffic and staged protests in several regions of France on Monday to demand better working conditions, officials of their union said.</p>
<p>Traffic reports said truck drivers set up roadblocks outside several cities. Others stopped work and left their trucks parked outside haulage companies.</p>
<p>The Workers Force (FO) trade union said a delegation of protesters would seek a meeting with a government official later in the day to spell out their grievances.</p>
<p>It was the second road transport protest this month. In earlier demonstrations, traffic in several cities was disrupted as demonstrators demanded cuts in taxes on diesel fuel.</p>
</text>
